\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate an acquisition claim}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{We formulate acquisition through a held-out transfer contrast because
training success alone does not distinguish learning from memorization,
selection, or evaluator exploitation. The base-versus-reinforcement-learning
comparisons in \citet{secs. 3--5}{yue2025does} motivate this distinction, but
their empirical criteria are not a universal definition of acquisition.}

\p{The thresholds in \ref{ftip-0007} make the finite evidential burden visible.
Follow-up results should state how many evaluation samples certify the two
inequalities, which distribution shifts preserve the witness, and which
counterexamples arise when the transfer evaluator leaks into training.}
